```
#include <iostream>

using namespace std;

int main()
{
    int num;
    cout << "Enter a number: ";
    cin >> num;
    int digital_root = num;
    // repeat until digital root is found
    while (digital_root > 9) {
        int sum = 0;
        // find the sum of digits
        while (digital_root != 0) {
            sum += digital_root % 10;
            digital_root /= 10;
        }
        digital_root = sum;
    }
    cout << "The digital root of " << num << " is: " << digital_root << endl;
    return 0;
}
```

In this program, we first prompt the user to enter a number. We initialize a variable `digital_root` to `num`, since initially the digital root of a number is itself. Then we enter a loop that keeps running until we arrive at the digital root of `num`. Inside the loop, we use another loop to find the sum of digits of `digital_root`. We repeatedly compute the remainder of `digital_root` divided by 10, which gives us the last digit of `digital_root`, and add it to a variable called `sum`. We then update the value of `digital_root` by dividing it by 10 to remove the last digit. Once we have added up all the digits, we set `digital_root` to the value of `sum`, and repeat the process until we arrive at a single-digit digital root. Finally, we print out the digital root of the original number.

