```
#include <iostream>
#include <string>

using namespace std;

int main()
{
    string input;
    cout << "Enter a number: ";
    cin >> input;
    int sum = 0;
    // loop through each character of the string
    for (char c : input) {
        // check if character is a digit
        if (isdigit(c)) {
            // convert character to integer and add to sum
            sum += c - '0';
        }
    }
    cout << "The sum of digits is: " << sum << endl;
    return 0;
}
```

In this program, we first prompt the user to enter a number as a string. We create a variable `sum` to store the sum of digits. We then loop through each character of the string using a range-based `for` loop. For each character, we check if it is a digit using the `isdigit` function. If it is a digit, we convert it from a character to an integer by subtracting the character for the digit '0'. We then add this integer to the `sum` variable. Once we have looped through all the characters of the string, we print out the sum of digits.

