import java.util.Scanner;

public class LongestCommonSubstring {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);

        // Prompt user for input
        System.out.print("Enter the first string: ");
        String str1 = scanner.nextLine().toLowerCase().replaceAll("[^a-z ]", "");
        System.out.print("Enter the second string: ");
        String str2 = scanner.nextLine().toLowerCase().replaceAll("[^a-z ]", "");

        // Calculate length of longest common substring
        int[][] table = new int[str1.length() + 1][str2.length() + 1];
        int maxLength = 0;
        for (int I = 1; I <= str1.length(); i++) {
            char c1 = str1.charAt(i - 1);
            for (int j = 1; j <= str2.length(); j++) {
                char c2 = str2.charAt(j - 1);
                if (c1 == c2) {
                    table[i][j] = table[i - 1][j - 1] + 1;
                    if (table[i][j] > maxLength) {
                        maxLength = table[i][j];
                    }
                } else {
                    table[i][j] = 0;
                }
            }
        }

        // Output result
        if (maxLength == 0) {
            System.out.println("There is no common substring.");
        } else {
            System.out.printf("The longest common substring has length %d.%n", maxLength);
        }
    }
}

Explanation of the implementation:

- The program starts by creating a Scanner object to read input from the user.
- The program prompts the user to enter two strings, and then reads those strings using the nextLine() method of Scanner.
- The strings are processed to lowercase and remove any character that is not a letter or a space using the toLowerCase() and replaceAll() methods respectively.
- To find the length of the longest common substring, the program uses dynamic programming. It creates a 2D table where table[i][j] represents the length of the longest common suffix of str1.substring(0, i) and str2.substring(0, j). The table is filled in a bottom-up fashion, and maxLength keeps track of the maximum value found in the table.
- Finally, the program outputs the result. If maxLength is 0, it means there is no common substring, and the program prints an appropriate message. Otherwise, it prints the length of the longest common substring using printf() with a format string.

