## Summary
This Perl script uses regular expressions to find all occurrences of a specific pattern (specified by the user) in a given directory and its subdirectories. The script supports case-insensitive searches and provides options for including/excluding certain file types (e.g. Only search .txt files). The output displays the filepath and line number of each occurrence or alternatively outputs the matched lines.

## Usage
```
perl find_pattern.pl -p "pattern" -d "/path/to/directory/" [-i] [-f ".txt"]
```
* `-p` (required): the pattern to search for
* `-d` (required): the directory to search in
* `-i` (optional): case-insensitive search (default is case-sensitive)
* `-f` (optional): file type filter (default is all files)

## Algorithm
1. Parse the command-line arguments
2. Recursively search the directory and its subdirectories for files that match the file type filter (if specified)
3. For each file found, open it and search for the specified pattern using regular expressions
4. Output either the filepath and line number of each occurrence or the matched lines (depending on user preference)

## Code

```perl
#!/usr/bin/perl
use strict;
use warnings;
use Getopt::Std;

# parse command-line arguments
my %opts;
getopts('p:d:if:', \%opts);
my $pattern = $opts{p} or die "Usage: $0 -p pattern -d directory [-i] [-f filetype]\n";
my $dir = $opts{d} or die "Usage: $0 -p pattern -d directory [-i] [-f filetype]\n";
my $case_insensitive = $opts{i};
my $file_type = $opts{f} || '.*';

# compile regular expression
my $regex = $case_insensitive ? qr/$pattern/i : qr/$pattern/;

# recursively search directory for files of specified type
sub search_files {
	my $dir = shift;
	opendir(my $dh, $dir) or die "Failed to open directory: $dir\n";
	my @files = grep { $_ ne '.' and $_ ne '..' } readdir $dh;
	closedir $dh;

	my @results;
	for my $file (@files) {
		my $path = "$dir/$file";
		if (-d $path) {
			push @results, search_files($path);
		} elsif ($file =~ /$file_type/) {
			push @results, search_file($path);
		}
	}
	return @results;
}

# search file for specified pattern
sub search_file {
	my $path = shift;
	open my $fh, '<', $path or die "Failed to open file: $path\n";
	my @results;
	while (my $line = <$fh>) {
		if ($line =~ /$regex/) {
			push @results, "$path:$.:$line";
		}
	}
	close $fh;
	return @results;
}

# display results
for my $result (search_files($dir)) {
	print "$result\n";
}
```

